## Hand of the Void

A hand of the void is a knot of arms with no body behind it, about the size of a person, purple and wet and never still; larger ones drag themselves along by their knuckles. They have no faces. Fingers curl and open where eyes would be, and they hunt by sound, turning toward whatever makes a noise and opening a mouth to spit a burst of violet liquid that burns where it lands.

They are slow, and quiet hides a body from them. Left alone they knit themselves back together from most harm, but a wound dealt by holy light will not close, and they go for whatever holds the most energy. They crawl out of the walls of the void place beyond a tear in the [[Phenomena/Weave|weave]].

One came back into the world through the tear that opened over the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]]'s dance floor. It was killed there, a holy spear wound from [[Org/The Scale/People/Ralph Bishop|Ralph Bishop]] of [[Org/The Scale/index|the Scale]] that would not close.

## Quailant

A Quailant is a behemoth of a void creature, gray-skinned and almost featureless. Its lower body is a three-legged, radial torso that walks like a tripod, and above it sits a matching three-limbed upper body, each arm bent at an angle no living thing would hold. On top is a smooth, empty face. It stalks back and forth before a [[Phenomena/Voidheart|Voidheart]] without touching it, and it can feed on a nearby person's feeling, leaving them slowed and heavy with despair.

One was lured out of the void when the Party pulled a Voidheart through a portal in the ruined town at the prow of the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]], and it crawled up after them as the Hands of the Void poured through the same hole.
